From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:57:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] GBA: give the cartridge quiet after a reset so it can finish
 connecting

Socket 2 now links on the bundled BIOS, socket 3 still does not, and the
telemetry shows why: socket 2 reached est=1 after nine reboots, socket 3
has taken forty-two and counting while the GameCube probes it about eight
thousand times.

Emerald's GameCubeMultiBoot_Main only re-runs its Init after roughly
eleven frames with no serial interrupt, and every joybus command clears
that counter. XD probes whichever socket it is waiting on continuously,
so the port it wants most is the one that never gets the quiet it needs:
the window opens, but the cartridge behind it is never ready and the
handshake never starts. A socket the game is not yet hammering gets that
quiet for free, which is why socket 2 works and socket 3 does not.

After an auto-reset, hold joybus commands back from that core until it has
reopened its window, with a six second ceiling so a core that never comes
back cannot wedge itself out of contact. Only the command is withheld --
the core is still time-synced and SI keeps its cadence, so the poll simply
reports "no GBA answered", which is what it already does while a core is
booting.
---
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
index ef38463563..9fa8548036 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.cpp
@@ -226,6 +226,15 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
         }
         m_last_auto_reset = m_timestamp_sent;
         m_data_cmd_count = 0;
+        // Emerald's GameCubeMultiBoot_Main only re-runs its Init after roughly
+        // eleven frames with no serial interrupt: every joybus command the
+        // GameCube sends resets that counter. XD probes a socket it is waiting
+        // on continuously (thousands of times per attempt), which starves the
+        // cartridge of the quiet it needs and leaves it never ready -- windows
+        // open, but the handshake never begins. Hold the commands back until
+        // this core has actually reopened its window, so the reboot lands in
+        // silence the way it does for a socket the game is not yet hammering.
+        m_quiet_until = m_timestamp_sent + tps * 6;
       }
     }
     // Diagnostic tap. Strictly a mirror of the state decided above -- no branch
@@ -245,7 +254,19 @@ int CSIDevice_GBAEmu::RunBuffer(u8* buffer, int request_length)
     m_diag_prev_link = link_now;
 
     m_link_was_enabled = link_now;
-    m_core->SendJoybusCommand(m_timestamp_sent, TransferInterval(), buffer, m_keys);
+
+    // The quiet window ends as soon as the link is back up (the cartridge has
+    // run its Init and is listening) or when it times out, so a core that never
+    // reopens can't wedge itself out of contact.
+    if (m_quiet_until != 0 && (link_now || m_timestamp_sent >= m_quiet_until))
+      m_quiet_until = 0;
+
+    // Withhold only the command itself. Everything below still runs, so the
+    // core keeps being time-synced and SI keeps its cadence; the poll simply
+    // finds no response and reports "no GBA answered", exactly as it already
+    // does while a core is booting.
+    if (m_quiet_until == 0)
+      m_core->SendJoybusCommand(m_timestamp_sent, TransferInterval(), buffer, m_keys);
 
     auto& si = m_system.GetSerialInterface();
     si.RemoveEvent(m_device_number);
diff --git a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
index e84ad8ab93..4e5778cf5e 100644
--- a/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
+++ b/Source/Core/Core/HW/SI/SI_DeviceGBAEmu.h
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ private:
   u64 m_last_data_cmd = 0;
   bool m_link_was_enabled = false;
   u64 m_last_link_seen = 0;
+  u64 m_quiet_until = 0;
   bool m_link_established = false;
   // Sustained joybus traffic means a real party exchange, not a stray probe.
   static constexpr u32 DATA_CMDS_FOR_BATTLE = 64;
